content.text:
Yes, and I think subagents are the better choice. A subagent also starts with a fresh context (just the brief), so the saving is the same. The integration is also much better:

- it shows up in your session's UI;
- the result comes back directly;
- it uses your subscription;
- 0.2.0 already ships the tier subagents with their model and effort.

I only moved to `claude -p` because the Codex reviews pushed for an OS sandbox around the helper. A subagent runs with the same permissions as your session, which is how you already work anyway. Dropping the sandbox also removes the whole sandbox, boundary-test and runner part of the build.

For Codex, subagents (`multi_agent`) are stable and enabled on your 0.158.0. I still need to check whether it lets us pick the model and effort per helper.

Want me to update the spec to use subagents on both harnesses, after checking that Codex point?

